original_sae_mgt_text:
The breeze is blowing across the bay.
      My lady, my lady;
  The ship that takes me far away,
      My lady, my lady;
  Old Master has sold me down the stream;
  They tell me 'tis not as bad as it seems,
      My lady, my lady.

  Of course I know that you'll be true,
      My lady, my lady;
  But then I do not know what to do,
      My lady, my lady;
  I knew some day we'd have to part,
  But then it puts me nigh breaks my heart,
      My lady, my lady.

  The day is long, the night is black,
      My lady, my lady;
  I know you'll wait till I come back,
      My lady, my lady;
  I'll stand the ship, I'll stand the chain,
  But I'll come back, my darling Jane,
      My lady, my lady.

  Just wait, just believe in what I say,
      My lady, my lady;
  There ain't nothing that can keep me away,
      My lady, my lady;
  A man's a man, and love is love;
  God knows our hearts, my little dove;
  He'll help us from his throne above,
      My lady, my lady.

