original_sae_mgt_text:
I have got religion, honey, and I'm happy as a king;
Everything I see about me is just like sunshine in the spring;
And it seems like I don't want to do another blessed thing
But just run and tell the neighbors, and to shout and pray and sing.

I have shaken my fist at Satan, and I've given the world my back;
I don't want no hindering causes now a-bothering in my track;
For I'm on my way to glory, and I feel too sure to miss.
Why, there ain't no use in sinning when religion's sweet as this.

Talk about a man backsliding when he's on the gospel way;
No, sir, I have beat the devil, and Temptation's lost the day.
Going to keep my eyes right straight up, going to shut my ears, and see
What old project Mister Satan's going to try to work on me.

Listen, what's that sound I hear there? It's no one commence to sing;
It's a fiddle; get away there! Don't you hear that blessed thing?
Why, that's sweet as dripping honey, 'cause, you know, I draw the bow,
And when music's sure enough music, I'm the one that's sure to know.

Why, I've done the double shuffle, 'til a body couldn't rest,
Just a-hearing Sam the fiddler play that tune his level best;
I could cut a mighty caper, I could give a mighty fling
Just right now, I'm more than certain I could cut the pigeon wing.

Look here, what's this I've been saying? What on earth's took hold of me?
That old music came nigh running my religion up a tree!
Clear out with that there old fiddle, don't you try that trick again;
Didn't think I could be tempted, but you like to made me sin!

