original_sae_mgt_text:
Oh, I just received a letter from the sweetest little gal;
        Oh, my; oh, my.
She's my lovely little sweetheart and her name is Sal:
        Oh, my; oh, my.
She writes me that she loves me and she loves me true,
She wonders if I'll tell her that I love her, too;
And my heart's so full of music that I don't know what to do;
        Oh, my; oh, my.

I got a man to read it and he read it fine;
        Oh, my; oh, my.
There ain't no use denying that her love is mine;
        Oh, my; oh, my.
But here's the thing that's putting me in such an awful plight,
I think of her at morning and I dream of her at night;
But how am I going to court her when I don't know how to write?
        Oh, my; oh, my.

My heart is bubbling over with the things I want to say;
        Oh, my; oh, my.
And there's lots of folks to copy what I tell them for the pay;
        Oh, my; oh, my.
But there's things that I am thinking that are only for her ears,
And I couldn't learn to write them if I took a dozen years;
So to go down there and tell her is the only way, it appears;
        Oh, my; oh, my.

